---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Information | GROUND ZERO"
  description="Information about the GROUND ZERO editorial portfolio."
>
  <section class="px-6 pb-16 pt-28 sm:px-8 sm:pb-24 sm:pt-32">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <p class="text-[0.68rem] uppercase tracking-[0.34em] text-stone-400">
          Information
        </p>
        <h1 class="max-w-sm text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
          A minimal framework for a restrained, image-led site.
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8 text-sm leading-7 text-stone-300">
        <p>
          GROUND ZERO is structured as an editorial portfolio with clear hierarchy, measured
          pacing, and a premium visual tone. The stack stays intentionally small: Astro,
          TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.
        </p>
        <p>
          The current setup provides a base layout, content collection support for projects, and
          two foundational pages that are easy to extend as design and content are refined.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-6 border-t border-white/10 pt-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <p class="text-[0.68rem] uppercase tracking-[0.34em] text-stone-500">Typography</p>
            <p class="mt-3">Satoshi as the primary voice, with Cormorant Garamond reserved for emphasis.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-[0.68rem] uppercase tracking-[0.34em] text-stone-500">Interaction</p>
            <p class="mt-3">Subtle hover darkening and fixed navigation, without parallax or animation libraries.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
